"W is the whole module.\",\"explanation\":\"No premise establishes W is nonzero, and no case handles W=0. For W=0 the claimed nonzero w cannot be chosen, while the target explicitly allows the zero subspace. The matrix-unit argument proves the result when W is nonzero, but not the universal assertion about all invariant subspaces. Consequently the sole producer and target closure cannot pass.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}}

